From: pocket-debs
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: MediaTek MT6785 DIP backend, autofocus and 3A extensions
Description:
 Use the ISP pass 2 (DIP) of the MediaTek MT6785 as the debayer stage of the
 software ISP, and extend the soft IPA for the main camera of the Moto G60s
 (OV64B40 with a voice coil lens). The CPU statistics, the soft IPA and the
 sensor controls stay in place; the DIP replaces the CPU or GPU debayering.
 .
 - Formats: MediaTek ISP packed 10-bit Bayer (Sxxxx10_MTISP, fourccs MBBA,
   MBGA, MBgA, MBRA, four pixels in five bytes, least significant bit first)
   in the format tables, the CPU debayer and the CPU statistics.
 - Debayer backend "mtk-dip" (software_isp.mode = mtk-dip): raw buffers go to
   the DIP by DMABUF, NV12 output buffers are allocated on the DIP and
   exported, DebayerParams become DIP parameter blocks (black level, white
   balance, colour matrix, tone curve); a params buffer carries only the
   blocks that changed. Without a usable DIP the software ISP falls back to
   the CPU. Option software_isp.dip_full_field: full field of view only.
 - DIP tuning (section "mtk-dip" of the soft IPA tuning file): tone curve,
   lens shading with a shadow lift, and the image quality blocks (edge
   enhancement, two luma/chroma noise reduction stages, demosaicing) per
   sensitivity with hysteresis, each block a dictionary with the fields of
   its UAPI struct. Optional blocks are sent disabled at stream start; the
   parameter buffer size follows the params node, blocks that do not fit go
   with the next buffer, a driver that refuses a block type falls back step
   by step.
 - Agc: mean target with digital gain, metering range, faster exposure steps,
   zone metering on a 5x5 grid; frame rate kept while the focus searches.
 - Awb: search along a colour temperature curve, grey zones.
 - Adjust: default saturation from the tuning file, per light level and
   colour temperature.
 - Af: contrast detect autofocus on a focus grid from the CPU statistics,
   climbing search from the current lens position, scene change detection,
   AfMode, AfTrigger, LensPosition, AfMetering and AfWindows (a list or a
   single rectangle, in pixel array active area coordinates, mapped through
   the analogue crop onto the sensor output frame).
 - CPU statistics: handed to the IPA by frame number, zone statistics, line
   pairs read through a cached copy, sparser sampling with a longer interval
   when the scene is settled, focus grid on demand.
 - Robustness: DelayedControls returns the latest queued values for frames
   beyond the queue; type checks of exposure, gain and lens position values.
 - The UAPI header of the DIP driver is a copy from its driver branch (not in
   the Linux kernel yet); unit tests for the formats, the parameter encoder
   and the fallback.
 .
 Applies on top of 0001 and 0003.
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (as the patched files); GPL-2.0-or-later for the
 tests and cam; the UAPI header copy is (GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR
 MIT
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
